    "analysis": "Jane directly avows that she loves Rochester, specifically asserting that her love is now greater than when he was proudly independent. The comparative and explanatory construction presents her emotional state as a considered truth. In the reunion context it also weakly renews relational devotion, but it does not itself clearly promise or undertake a future obligation.",
